bug_fixes.problem_statement:
Support literal types
Support for the [literal type annotation](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0586/) should be added. Example:

```python

@dataclass
class ImageMetadata(JsonSchemaMixin):
    width: int
    height: int
    bits_per_pixel: Literal[8, 16, 24]
```

Generates the following schema:
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "width",
    "height",
    "bits_per_pixel"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "width": {
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "height": {
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "bits_per_pixel": {
      "type": "integer",
      "enum": [8, 16, 24]
    }
  },
}
```

Support nullable fields
There should be an option to allow nullable fields. I propose the following api:

```python
@dataclass
class Address(JsonSchemaMixin):
    company: Optional[str] = field(default=None, metadata=dict(nullable=True))
    building: str
    street: str
    ...
```

There are a couple of ways to support nullable fields in JSON schema, either:

```json
{
  "properties": {
    "company": {"type": ["string", "null"]}
  }
}
```
or:
```json
{
  "properties": {
    "company": {"oneOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}]}
  }
}
```
The former is not supported in Swagger / OpenAPI though. OpenAPI 3 also supports the following:
```json
{
  "properties": {
    "company": {"type": "string", "nullable": true}
  }
}
```

freezegun 1.5.4 crashes if parametrized argument is called "func"
Likely introduced by this commit: https://github.com/spulec/freezegun/commit/10c93f2d6c98f82e54470b05144cd0f17d3e1b46

Reproducer:

```python
import datetime
import freezegun
import pytest

@pytest.mark.parametrize("func", ("a", "b"))
@freezegun.freeze_time(datetime.datetime.now())
def test_freezegun_crashes(func):
    print(func)

@pytest.mark.parametrize("arg", ("a", "b"))
@freezegun.freeze_time(datetime.datetime.now())
def test_freezegun_does_not_crash(arg):
    print(arg)
```

If a test has an argument called `func`, pytest will crash:

```
item = <Function test_freezegun_crashes[a]>

    @pytest.hookimpl(wrapper=True, tryfirst=True)
    def pytest_runtest_call(item):
>       result = yield

/path/to/venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pytestqt/plugin.py:189: 
_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ 

args = (), kwargs = {'func': 'a'}, time_factory = <freezegun.api.FrozenDateTimeFactory object at 0x727db48800d0>

    @functools.wraps(func)
    def wrapper(*args: "P.args", **kwargs: "P.kwargs") -> T:
        with self as time_factory:
>           return self._call_with_time_factory(time_factory, func, *args, **kwargs)
E           TypeError: _freeze_time._call_with_time_factory() got multiple values for argument 'func'
```

